- Tempo & Pulse: Variable rubato shifting into frenetic 110–160 BPM, driven by syncopated polyrhythms, unmetered free-jazz percussion, and cyclic signal clicks.
- Harmonic Palette: Indian classical microtonal Ragas (such as Bhairav and Marwa) warped by avant-garde chromatic dissonances, extended saxophone cluster tones, and drone-heavy modal shifts.
- Production Signatures: Tape-flanged sitar resonances routed through vintage oil-can delays, field-recorded electromagnetic hums from traffic control boxes used as low-end drones, and extreme stereo-panning of overblown woodwinds.
- Dynamics: Volatile and expansive; quiet, shimmering sitar drones suddenly detonate into wall-of-sound free improvisation before dissolving into liquid, tape-mangled spatial feedback.

